1123   
1124  *------------------------------------------------------------------
1125  * 1.5.1  Declare calibration parameters, including base year values
1126  *------------------------------------------------------------------
1127   
1128  *For model calibration, one parameter is created for each model variable with the suffix "0" added to the variable name.
1129  *  0 is also added to the names of parameters whose values are changed in experiments.
1130   
1131  PARAMETERS
1132  *Model parameters base year values
1133   alphaf0(F,A)       productivity shift for factor F in activity A
1134   alphava0(A)        shift parameter for CES activity production function
1135   betah0(A,H)        marginal share of household consumption on home commodity C from activity A
1136   betam0(C,H)        marginal share of household consumption on marketed commodity C
1137   gammah0(A,H)       per-capita subsistence consumption for household H on home commodity C for activity A
1138   gammam0(C,H)       per-capita subsistence consumption of marketed commodity C for household H
1139   icd0(C,CP)         trade input of C per unit of commodity CP produced & sold domestically
1140   ice0(C,CP)         trade input of C per unit of commodity CP exported
1141   icm0(C,CP)         trade input of C per unit of commodity CP imported
1142   pop0(H)            total population of workers and non-workers in household H
1143   pwe0(C)            world price of exports
1144   pwm0(C)            world price of imports
1145   qbarg0(C)          exogenous (unscaled) government demand
1146   qbarinv0(C)        exogenous (unscaled) investment demand
1147   qdst0(C)           inventory investment by sector of origin
1148   shif0(AC,ACP)      share of institution INS (incl. rest of world) in post-tax income of factor F
1149   shii0(AC,ACP)      share of institution INS in post-tax post-savings income of institution INSP
1150   trnsf0(F,INS)      transfers from factor F to institution INS (including rest of world)
1151   trnsi0(INS,INSP)   transfers from institution INS) to institution INSP (including rest of world)
1152  *Model variables    base year values
1153   CPI0               consumer price index (PQ-based)
1154   DMPS0              change in marginal propensity to save for selected institution
1155   DPI0               index for domestic producer prices (PDS-based)
1156   DTA0               additive activity tax (TA) adjustment
1157   DTE0               additive export tax (TE) adjustment
1158   DTF0               additive direct factor tax (TF) adjustment
1159   DTI0               additive domestic institution tax (TI) adjustment
1160   DTM0               additive import tariff (TM) adjustment
1161   DTQ0               additive sales tax (TQ) adjustment
1162   DTV0               additive value-added tax (TV) adjustment
1163   EG0                total current government expenditure
1164   EH0(H)             household consumption expenditure
1165   EXR0               exchange rate
1166   FSAV0              foreign savings
1167   GADJ0              government demand scaling factor
1168   GOVSHR0            government consumption share of absorption
1169   GSAV0              government savings
1170   IADJ0              investment scaling factor (for fixed capital formation)
1171   INVSHR0            investment share of absorption
1172   MPS0(AC)           marginal propensity to save for domestic non-government institution INS
1173   MPSADJ0            savings rate (MPS) scaling factor
1174   PA0(A)             output price of activity A
1175   PDD0(C)            demand price for commodity C produced and sold domestically
1176   PDS0(C)            supply price for commodity C produced and sold domestically
1177   PE0(C)             price of export aggregate to producer excluding transport costs
1178   PINTA0(A)          price of intermediate aggregate
1179   PM0(C)             price of import aggregate to demander including transport costs
1180   PQ0(C)             price of composite commodity C
1181   PSAV0              total private savings
1182   PVA0(A)            value added price
1183   PX0(C)             average output price
1184   PXAC0(A,C)         price of commodity C from activity A
1185   QA0(A)             level of domestic activity
1186   QD0(C)             quantity of domestic sales
1187   QE0(C)             quantity of exports
1188   QF0(F,A)           quantity demanded of factor F from activity A
1189   QFS0(F)            quantity of factor supply
1190   QG0(C)             quantity of government consumption
1191   QH0(C,H)           quantity consumed of marketed commodity C by household H
1192   QHA0(A,H)          quantity consumed of home activity A by household H
1193   QINT0(C,A)         quantity of intermediate demand for commodity C from activity A
1194   QINTA0(A)          quantity of aggregate intermediate input
1195   QINV0(C)           quantity of fixed investment demand
1196   QM0(C)             quantity of imports
1197   QQ0(C)             quantity of composite goods supply
1198   QT0(C)             quantity of trade and transport demand for commodity C
1199   QVA0(A)            quantity of aggregate value added
1200   QX0(C)             quantity of aggregate marketed commodity output
1201   QXAC0(A,C)         quantity of ouput of commodity C from activity A
1202   TA0(A)             activity tax rates
1203   TAADJ0             activity tax (TA) scaling factor
1204   TABS0              total absorption
1205   TE0(C)             export tax rates
1206   TEADJ0             export tax (TE) scaling factor
1207   TF0(F)             direct factor tax rates
1208   TFADJ0             factor tax (TF) scaling factor
1209   TI0(AC)            direct tax rates on domestic institutions INSD
1210   TIADJ0             direct tax (TI) scaling factor
1211   TM0(C)             import tariff rates
1212   TMADJ0             import tariff (TM) scaling factor
1213   TRII0(AC,ACP)      transfers from column institutions INSF to row institutions INS
1214   TQ0(C)             composite commodity taxes
1215   TQADJ0             composite commodity tax (TQ) scaling factor
1216   TV0(A)             value-added tax rates
1217   TVADJ0             value-added tax (TV) scaling factor
1218   WALRAS0            savings-investment imbalance (should be zero)
1219   WF0(F)             economy-wide wage (rent) for factor F
1220   WFDIST0(F,A)       wage distortion variable for factor F in activity A
1221   YF0(F)             factor income from activities
1222   YG0                total government income
1223   YIF0(INS,F)        income of institution INS from factor F
1224   YI0(INS)           income of domestic non-government institution INS
1225  ;
1226   
1227   
1228  *------------------ ------------------------------------------------
1229  * 1.5.2  Prices and quantities
1230  *------------------------------------------------------------------
1231   
       The prices PDS, PX, and PE  may be initialized at any desired price. The user may prefer to initialize these prices at
       unity or, if he/she is interested in tracking commodity flows in physical units, at commodity-specific, observed prices
       (per physical unit). For any given commodity, these three prices should be identical. Initialization at observed prices
       may be attractive for disaggregated agricultural commodities. If so, the corresponding quantity values reflect physical
       units (given the initial price).
       
       The remaining supply-side price, PXAC, and the non-commodity prices, EXR and PA may be initizalized at any desired
       level. In practice, it may be preferable to initialize PXAC at the relevant supply-side price and EXR and PA at unity.
       
       If physical units are used, the user should select the unit (tons vs. '000 tons) so that initial price and quantity
       variables are reasonably scaled (for example between 1.0E-2 and 1.0E+3) -- bad scaling may cause solver problems.
       Initialization at unity should cause no problem as long as the initial SAM is reasonably scaled.
1246   
1247  PARAMETER
1248   PSUP(C)            initial supply-side market price for commodity C
1249   SHCTD(C)           share of commodity CT in transaction services for domestic sales
1250   SHCTE(C)           share of commodity CT in transaction services for exports
1251   SHCTM(C)           share of commodity CT in transaction services for imports
1252  ;
1253   
1254   PSUP(C)               = 1;
1255   PE0(C)$CE(C)          = PSUP(C);
1256   PX0(C)$CX(C)          = PSUP(C);
1257   PDS0(C)$CD(C)         = PSUP(C);
1258   PXAC0(A,C)$SAM(A,C)   = PSUP(C);
1259   PA0(A)$SAM('TOTAL',A) = 1;
1260   
       The exchange rate may be initialized at unity, in which case all data are in foreign currency units (FCU; e.g.,
       dollars). Set the exchange rate at another value to differentiate foreign exchange transactions, which will be valued
       in FCU, and domestic transactions valued in local currency units (LCU). The SAM is assumed to be valued in LCU, and
       the exchange rate is then used to calculate FCU values for transactions with the rest of the world.
1267   
1268   EXR0 = EXRBASE;
1269   
1270  *Activity quantity = payment to activity divided by activity price.
1271  *  QA covers both on-farm consumption and marketed output output GROSS of tax.
1272   QA0(A)$PA0(A) = SAM('TOTAL',A)/PA0(A);
1273   
1274  *Unit value-added price = total value-added / activity quantity define QVA0 and PVA0 gross of factor taxes.
1275   QVA0(A)               = SUM(F, SAM(F,A)) + TAXPAR('VATTAX',A);
1276   PVA0(A)$QVA0(A)       = (SUM(F, SAM(F,A)) + TAXPAR('VATTAX',A))/QVA0(A);
1277   iva(A)$QA0(A)         = QVA0(A)/QA0(A);
1278   QXAC0(A,C)$PXAC0(A,C) = SAM(A,C)/PXAC0(A,C);
1279   
1280  *Home consumption of activity output
1281   QHA0(A,H)$PA0(A) = SAM(A,H)/PA0(A);
1282   
1283  *Output quantity = value received by producers divided by producer price.
1284  *  QX covers only marketed output.
1285   QX0(C)$SUM(A, SAM(A,C)) = SUM(A, SAM(A,C)) / PX0(C);
1286   
1287  *Export quantity = export revenue received by producers (ie. minus tax and transactions cost) divided by export price.
1288   QE0(C)$CE(C) = (SAM(C,RW) - TAXPAR('EXPTAX',C) - SAM(CTE,C))/PE0(C);
1289   
1290  *World export price = rest of world export payment (in foreign currency) / export quantity.
1291   pwe0(C)$CE(C) = (SAM(C,RW)/EXR0) / QE0(C);
1292   pwe(C)        = pwe0(C);
1293   
1294  *Export taxes and adjustment factors
1295   TE0(C)$CE(C)  = TAXPAR('EXPTAX',C)/SAM(C,RW);
1296   TEADJ0        = 0;
1297   DTE0          = 0;
1298   te01(C)$CE(C) = 1;
1299   tebar(C)      = TE0(C);
1300   
1301  *Quantity of output sold domestically = output quantity less quantity exported = value of domestic sales divided by
1302  *  domestic supply price. QD0 covers only marketed output.
1303   QD0(C)$CD(C) = QX0(C) - QE0(C);
1304   
1305  *Domestic demander price = demander payment divided by quantity bought.
1306   PDD0(C)$QD0(C) = (PDS0(C)*QD0(C) + SAM(CTD,C))/QD0(C);
1307   
1308  *Define import price to equal domestic price so that import and domestic units are the same to the purchaser.
1309  *  If no domestic good, set PM to 1.
1310   PM0(CM) = PDD0(CM);
1311   PM0(CM)$(QD0(CM) EQ 0) = 1;
1312   
1313  *Import quantity = demander payment for imports (including tariffs and marketing cost) divided by demander price.
1314   QM0(C)$CM(C) = (SAM(RW,C) + TAXPAR('IMPTAX',C) + SAM(CTM,C))/PM0(C);
1315   
1316  *World import price = import value (in foreign currency) / import quantity.
1317   pwm0(C)$CM(C) = (SAM(RW,C)/EXR0) / QM0(C);
1318   pwm(C) = pwm0(C);
1319   
1320  *Import taxes and adjustment factors.
1321   TM0(C)$CM(C) = TAXPAR('IMPTAX',C)/ SAM(RW,C);
1322   TMADJ0 = 0;
1323   DTM0 = 0;
1324   tm01(C) = 1;
1325   tmbar(C) = TM0(C);
1326   
1327  *Composite supply is the sum of domestic market sales and imports (since they are initialized at the same price).
1328   QQ0(C)$(CD(C) OR CM(C)) = QD0(C) + QM0(C) ;
1329   PQ0(C)$QQ0(C) = (SAM(C,'TOTAL') - SAM(C,RW))/QQ0(C);
1330   
1331  *Sales taxes and adjustment factors.
1332   TQ0(C)$QQ0(C) = TAXPAR('COMTAX',C)/(PQ0(C)*QQ0(C));
1333   TQADJ0 = 0;
1334   DTQ0 = 0;
1335   tq01(C) = 1;
1336   tqbar(C) = TQ0(C);
1337   
1338  *The following code works when for any number of sectors providing transactions services, as well as for the case when
1339  *  they are not in the SAM.
1340   SHCTD(CT) = SAM(CT,CTD)/SAM('TOTAL',CTD);
1341   SHCTM(CT) = SAM(CT,CTM)/SAM('TOTAL',CTM);
1342   SHCTE(CT) = SAM(CT,CTE)/SAM('TOTAL',CTE);
1343   
1344  *Transactions input coefficients
1345   icd0(CT,C)$QD0(C) = (SHCTD(CT)*SAM(CTD,C)/PQ0(CT)) / QD0(C);
1346   ice0(CT,C)$QE0(C) = (SHCTM(CT)*SAM(CTE,C)/PQ0(CT)) / QE0(C);
1347   icm0(CT,C)$QM0(C) = (SHCTE(CT)*SAM(CTM,C)/PQ0(CT)) / QM0(C);
1348   
1349   icd(CT,C) = icd0(CT,C);
1350   ice(CT,C) = ice0(CT,C);
1351   icm(CT,C) = icm0(CT,C);
1352   
1353  *Value added taxes. Indirect activity tax rate = tax payment / output value. Tax is here applied to total output value
1354  *  (including own consumption).
1355   TV0(A)$(PVA0(A)*QVA0(A)) = TAXPAR('VATTAX',A) / (PVA0(A)*QVA0(A));
1356   TVADJ0 = 0;
1357   DTV0 = 0;
1358   tv01(A) = 1;
1359   tvbar(A) = tv0(A);
1360   
1361  *Activity taxes and adjustment factors. QA is GROSS of tax, so base for TA is as well.
1362   TA0(A)$SAM(A,'TOTAL') = TAXPAR('ACTTAX',A) / SAM(A,'TOTAL');
1363   DTA0 = 0;
1364   TAADJ0 = 0;
1365   ta01(A) = 1;
1366   tabar(A) = ta0(A);
1367   
1368  *Yield coefficient for C-to-A linear aggregation (ACCES(A) = NO). Net out home consumption of activity A before aggregating.
1369  *   Yield coefficient = quantity produced less home-consumed output / activity quantity less home-consumed output.
1370   theta(A,C)$(PXAC0(A,C) AND (QA0(A) - SUM(H, SAM(A,H)))) = (SAM(A,C)/PXAC0(A,C)) / (QA0(A) - SUM(H, SAM(A,H)));
1371   
1372  *Intermediate input coefficient = input use / output quantity.
1373   QINTA0(A) = SUM(C$PQ0(C), SAM(C,A)/PQ0(C));
1374   
1375   ica(C,A)$(PQ0(C) AND QINTA0(A)) = (SAM(C,A)/PQ0(C)) / QINTA0(A);
1376   
1377   inta(A)$QA0(A) = QINTA0(A) / QA0(A);
1378   pinta0(A)      = SUM(C, ica(C,A)*PQ0(C));
1379   
1380  *CPI weight by commodity = household consumption value for commodity / total household consumption value.
1381  *  CPI does not consider on-farm consumption.
1382   cwts(C)$SUM((CP,H), SAM(CP,H)) = SUM(H, SAM(C,H)) / SUM((CP,H), SAM(CP,H));
1383   
1384  *Domestic sales price index weight = domestic sales value for commodity / total domestic salues value.
1385  *  Domestic sales price index does not consider on-farm consumption.
1386   dwts(C) = (SUM(A, SAM(A,C)) - (SAM(C,RW) - SUM(cte, SAM(cte,C))))/
1387              SUM(CP, SUM(A, SAM(A,CP)) - (SAM(CP,RW) - SUM(cte, SAM(cte,CP))));
1388   
1389   CPI0    = SUM(C, cwts(C)*PQ0(C));
1390   DPI0    = SUM(CD, dwts(CD)*PDS0(CD)) ;
1391   
1392   
1393  *------------------------------------------------------------------
1394  * 1.5.3  Production and trade
1395  *------------------------------------------------------------------
1396   
1397  PARAMETER
1398   WFA(F,A)           wage for factor f in activity a (used for calibration)
1399   predeltaa(A)       dummy used to define deltaa
1400   predelta(C)        dummy used to define deltaq
1401  ;
1402   
1403  *Compute exponents from elasticites
1404   rhoa(A)$(AA(A) AND ACES(A))   = (1/AELAS(A,'ELASPRD2')) - 1;
1405   rhoac(C)$CELAS(C,'ELASAC')    =  1/CELAS(C,'ELASAC')    - 1;
1406   rhoca(A)$(AA(A) AND ACCES(A)) = (1/AELAS(A,'ELASCA'))   + 1;
1407   rhoq(C)$(CM(C) AND CD(C))     = (1/CELAS(C,'SIGMAQ'))   - 1;
1408   rhot(C)$(CE(C) AND CD(C))     = (1/CELAS(C,'SIGMAT'))   + 1;
1409   rhova(A)$AA(A)                = (1/AELAS(A,'ELASPRD'))  - 1;
1410   
1411  *CES aggregation of domestic output from different activities.
1412   deltaac(A,C)$(SAM(A,C) AND CELAS(C,'ELASAC')) = (PXAC0(A,C)*QXAC0(A,C)**(1/CELAS(C,'ELASAC')))/SUM(AP, PXAC0(AP,C)*QXAC0(AP,C)**(1/CELAS(C,'ELASAC')));
1413   alphaac(C)$SUM(A,deltaac(A,C)) = QX0(C)/(SUM(A$deltaac(A,C), deltaac(A,C) * QXAC0(A,C)**(-rhoac(C))) )**(-1/rhoac(C));
1414   
1415  *CET disaggregation of domestic output to different commodities.
1416   deltaca(A,C)$QXAC0(A,C) = (PXAC0(A,C)*(QXAC0(A,C))**(1-rhoca(A))) / SUM(CP$QXAC0(A,CP), PXAC0(A,CP)*(QXAC0(A,CP))**(1-rhoca(A)));
1417   alphaca(A)$ACCES(A)     = (QA0(A) - SUM(H, QHA0(A,H))) / (SUM(C$deltaca(A,C), deltaca(A,C)*QXAC0(A,C)**rhoca(A)))**(1/rhoca(A));
1418   
1419  *Defining factor employment and supply.
1420   QF0(F,A) = QF2BASE(F,A);
1421   QFS0(F)  = SUM(A, QF0(F,A));
1422   
1423  *Economy-wide wage average is total factor income over employment.
1424   WF0(F)$SUM(A, QF0(F,A)) = SUM(A, SAM(F,A))/SUM(A, QF0(F,A));
1425   
1426  *Wage distortion factor.
1427   WFA(F,A)$SAM(F,A)     = SAM(F,A)/QF0(F,A);
1428   WFDIST0(F,A)$SAM(F,A) = WFA(F,A)/WF0(F);
1429   
1430  *CES activity production function.
1431   deltava(F,A)$QF0(F,A) = (WFDIST0(F,A)*WF0(F)*(QF0(F,A))**(1+rhova(A))) / SUM(FP, WFDIST0(FP,A)*WF0(FP)*(QF0(FP,A))**(1+rhova(A)));
1432   alphava0(A)$QVA0(A) = QVA0(A)/(SUM(F$(QF0(F,A)), deltava(F,A)*QF0(F,A)**(-rhova(A))))**(-1/rhova(A));
1433   alphava(A)   = alphava0(A);
1434   alphaf0(F,A) = 1;
1435   alphaf(F,A)  = alphaf0(F,A);
1436   
1437  *CES top level production function.
1438   predeltaa(A) = 0 ;
1439   predeltaa(A)$(ACES(A) AND QINTA0(A)) = (PVA0(A)/PINTA0(A))*(QVA0(A)/QINTA0(A))**(1+rhoa(A));
1440   deltaa(A)$ACES(A) = predeltaa(A)/(1 + predeltaa(A)) ;
1441   alphaa(A)$deltaa(A) = QA0(A)/((deltaa(A)*QVA0(A)**(-rhoa(A)) + (1-deltaa(A))*QINTA0(A)**(-rhoa(A)))**(-1/rhoa(A)));
1442   
1443  *Intermediate demand.
1444   QINT0(C,A)$PQ0(C) = SAM(C,A) / PQ0(C);
1445   
1446  *Transactions demand.
1447   QT0(CT)$PQ0(CT) = (SUM(CTD, SAM(CT,CTD)) + SUM(CTE, SAM(CT,CTE)) + SUM(CTM, SAM(CT,CTM))) / PQ0(CT);
1448   
1449  *CET transformation.
1450   deltat(C)$(CE(C) AND CD(C)) = 1 / (1 + PDS0(C)/PE0(C)*(QE0(C)/QD0(C))**(rhot(C)-1));
1451   
1452   alphat(C)$(CE(C) AND CD(C)) = QX0(C) / (deltat(C)*QE0(C)**rhot(C) + (1-deltat(C))*QD0(C)**rhot(C))**(1/rhot(C));
1453   
1454  *Armington aggregation.
1455   predelta(C)$(CM(C) AND CD(C)) = (PM0(C)/(PDD0(C)))*(QM0(C)/QD0(C))**(1+rhoq(C));
1456   deltaq(C)$(CM(C) AND CD(C)) = predelta(C)/(1 + predelta(C));
1457   alphaq(C)$(CM(C) AND CD(C)) = QQ0(C)/(deltaq(C)*QM0(C)**(-rhoq(C)) + (1-deltaq(C))*QD0(C)**(-rhoq(C)))**(-1/rhoq(C));
1458   
1459   
1460  *------------------------------------------------------------------
1461  * 1.5.4  Institutions
1462  *------------------------------------------------------------------
1463   
1464  *Factor income by factor category from activities (value added).
1465   YF0(F) = SUM(A, SAM(F,A)) + SAM(F,GV) + SAM(F,RW);
1466   
1467  *Exogenous transfers (in local currency) from factors F to government.
1468   trnsf0(F,GV) = SAM(F,GV)/CPI0;
1469   
1470  *Exogenous transfers (in foreign currency) from factors F to rest of world.
1471   trnsf0(F,RW) = SAM(F,RW)/EXR0;
1472   
1473  *Factor payments to institutions (including rest of world).
1474   YIF0(INS,F) = SAM(INS,F);
1475   
1476  *Shares of institutions in factor income (net of factor taxes).
1477   shif0(INS,F)$(SAM(F,'TOTAL') - TAXPAR('FACTAX',F)) = SAM(INS,F)/(SAM(F,'TOTAL') - TAXPAR('FACTAX',F));
1478   shif(INS,F) = shif0(INS,F);
1479   
1480  *Factor taxes
1481   TF0(F)$YF0(F) = TAXPAR('FACTAX',F)/YF0(F);
1482   DTF0     = 0;
1483   TFADJ0   = 0;
1484   tf01(F)  = 1;
1485   tfbar(F) = tf0(F);
1486   
1487  *Total income for domestic non-government institutions (includes transfers from government and rest of world).
1488   YI0(INSDNG) = SAM('TOTAL',INSDNG);
1489   
1490  *Exogenous transfers (in foreign currency) from rest of world to domestic institutions INSD.
1491   trnsi0(INSD,RW) = SAM(INSD,RW)/EXR0;
1492   
1493  *Exogenous transfers (in local currency) from government to domestic institutions INSD.
1494   trnsi0(INSD,GV) = SAM(INSD,GV)/CPI0;
1495   
1496  *Exogenous transfers (in foreign currency) from government to rest of world.
1497   trnsi0(RW,GV) = SAM(RW,GV)/EXR0;
1498   
1499   trnsf(F,INS)    = trnsf0(F,INS);
1500   trnsi(INS,INSP) = trnsi0(INS,INSP);
1501   
1502  *Endogenous transfers from domestic non-government institutions to institutions INS (including rest of world).
1503   TRII0(INS,INSDNG) = SAM(INS,INSDNG);
1504   
1505  *Share of institution INS in income of domestic non-government institutions (net of direct taxes and savings).
1506   shii0(INS,INSDNG)$(SAM('TOTAL',INSDNG) - TAXPAR('INSTAX',INSDNG) - SAM(SI,INSDNG))
1507           = SAM(INS,INSDNG) / (SAM('TOTAL',INSDNG) - TAXPAR('INSTAX',INSDNG) - SAM(SI,INSDNG));
1508   shii(AC,ACP) = shii0(AC,ACP);
1509   
1510  *Direct tax rates.
1511   TI0(INSDNG)$SAM('TOTAL',INSDNG) = TAXPAR('INSTAX',INSDNG)/SAM('TOTAL',INSDNG);
1512   DTI0          = 0;
1513   TIADJ0        = 0;
1514   ti01(INSDNG)  = 1;
1515   tibar(INSDNG) = TI0(INSDNG);
1516   
1517  *Savings rates (share of disposable post-tax income).
1518   MPS0(INSDNG)$SAM('TOTAL',INSDNG) = SAM(SI,INSDNG)/(SAM('TOTAL',INSDNG) - TAXPAR('INSTAX',INSDNG));
1519   DMPS0          = 0;
1520   MPSADJ0        = 0;
1521   mps01(INSDNG)  = 1;
1522   mpsbar(INSDNG) = MPS0(INSDNG);
1523   
1524  *Household consumption spending and consumption quantities.
1525  *  QH is total, not per capita.
1526   EH0(H)          = SUM(C, SAM(C,H)) + SUM(A, SAM(A,H));
1527   QH0(C,H)$PQ0(C) = SAM(C,H) / PQ0(C);
1528   
1529  *Government indicators.
1530   YG0           = SAM('TOTAL',GV);
1531   EG0           = SAM('TOTAL',GV) - SAM(SI,GV);
1532   QG0(C)$PQ0(C) = SAM(C,GV)/PQ0(C);
1533   qbarg0(C)     = QG0(C);
1534   qbarg(C)      = qbarg0(C);
1535   GADJ0         = 1;
1536   GSAV0         = SAM(SI,GV);
1537   
1538   
1539  *------------------------------------------------------------------
1540  * 1.5.5  LES calibration
1541  *------------------------------------------------------------------
1542   
1543  PARAMETERS
1544  *Calibration
1545   BUDSHR(C,H)        budget share for marketed commodity C and household H
1546   BUDSHR2(A,H)       budget share for home consumption of activity A and household H
1547   BUDSHRCHK(H)       check that budget shares some to unity
1548   ELASCHK(*,H)       check that expenditure elasticities satisfy Engel aggregation
1549  *Checking
1550   SUPERNUM(H)        LES supernumerary income
1551   FRISCH2(H)         alternative definition of Frisch (ratio of consumption to supernumerary consumption)
1552   LESCHK(H)          check on LES parameter definitions (error message)
1553   SUPERNUMR(H)       ratio of supernumerary income to total household consumption expenditure EH
1554   PELAS(AC,H)        own price elasticity for home consumed activities A and marketed commodities C
1555  ;
1556   
1557   BUDSHR(C,H)$EH0(H)  = SAM(C,H)/EH0(H);
1558   BUDSHR2(A,H)$EH0(H) = SAM(A,H)/EH0(H);
1559   
1560   BUDSHRCHK(H) = SUM(C, BUDSHR(C,H)) + SUM(A, BUDSHR2(A,H)) - 1;
1561   BUDSHRCHK(H)$(ABS(BUDSHRCHK(H)) LT 1E-6) = 0;
1562   
1563   ELASCHK('1',H) = (SUM(C, BUDSHR(C,H)*HELAS(C,H)) + SUM(A, BUDSHR2(A,H)*HELAS(A,H))) - 1;
1564   ELASCHK('1',H)$(ABS(ELASCHK('1',H)) LT 1E-6) = 0;
1565   
1566  *Correct elasticities to make them satisfy Engle aggregation exactly.
1567   HELAS(AC,H)$(ELASCHK('1',H) + 1) = HELAS(AC,H)/(ELASCHK('1',H) + 1);
1568   
1569  *Check Engel aggregation again after possible corrections.
1570   ELASCHK('2',H) = (SUM(C, BUDSHR(C,H)*HELAS(C,H)) + SUM(A, BUDSHR2(A,H)*HELAS(A,H))) - 1;
1571   ELASCHK('2',H)$(ABS(ELASCHK('2',H)) LT 1E-6) = 0;
1572   
1573  *Marginal share of household consumption on marketed commodities and home activities.
1574   betam0(C,H) = BUDSHR(C,H)*HELAS(C,H);
1575   betah0(A,H) = BUDSHR2(A,H)*HELAS(A,H);
1576   betam(C,H)  = betam0(C,H);
1577   betah(A,H)  = betah0(A,H);
1578   
1579  *Household populations.
1580   pop0(H) = HPOP(H)*POPSCALE;
1581   pop(H)  = pop0(H);
1582   
1583  *Per-capita subsistence consumption for household H on home activities and marketed commodities.
1584   gammam0(C,H)$BUDSHR(C,H)
1585           = ((SUM(CP, SAM(CP,H))/pop(H) + [SUM(AP, QHA0(AP,H)*PA0(AP))/hpop(H)]) / PQ0(C))
1586           * (BUDSHR(C,H) + betam(C,H)/FRISCH(H));
1587   gammah0(A,H)$BUDSHR2(A,H)
1588           = ((SUM(CP, SAM(CP,H))/pop(H) + [SUM(AP, QHA0(AP,H)*PA0(AP))/hpop(H)]) / PA0(A))
1589           * (BUDSHR2(A,H) + betah(A,H)/FRISCH(H));
1590   gammam(C,H) = gammam0(C,H);
1591   gammah(A,H) = gammah0(A,H);
1592   
1593  *Checking LES parameters.
1594  *   LES supernumerary income.
1595   SUPERNUM(H) = EH0(H) - pop(H) * (SUM(A, gammah(A,H)*PA0(A)) + SUM(C, gammam(C,H)*PQ0(C)));
1596  *   Ratio of supernumerary income to total household consumption expenditure EH.
1597   SUPERNUMR(H)$EH0(H) = SUPERNUM(H)/EH0(H);
1598  *   Alternative definition of Frisch (ratio of consumption to supernumerary consumption).
1599   FRISCH2(H)$SUPERNUM(H) = -EH0(H)/SUPERNUM(H);
1600  *   Check on LES parameter definitions (error message).
1601   LESCHK(H) = FRISCH(H) - FRISCH2(H);
1602  *   Own price elasticity for home consumed activities A and marketed commodities C.
1603   PELAS(C,H)$QH0(C,H)  = -HELAS(C,H)*( PQ0(C)*gammam(C,H) / (SUM(CP, SAM(CP,H)) + SUM(AP, SAM(AP,H))) - 1/FRISCH(H));
1604   PELAS(A,H)$QHA0(A,H) = -HELAS(A,H)*( PA0(A)*gammah(A,H) / (SUM(CP, SAM(CP,H)) + SUM(AP, SAM(AP,H))) - 1/FRISCH(H));
1605   
1606  *------------------------------------------------------------------
1607  * 1.5.6  System constraints
1608  *------------------------------------------------------------------
1609   
1610  *Fixed capital formation indicators.
1611   QINV0(C)$PQ0(C) = SAM(C,SI)/PQ0(C);
1612   qbarinv0(C)     = QINV0(C);
1613   qbarinv(C)      = qbarinv0(C);
1614   IADJ0           = 1 ;
1615   
1616  *Stock changes.
1617   qdst0(C)$PQ0(C) = SAM(C,STK)/PQ0(C);
1618   qdst(C)         = qdst0(C);
1619   
1620  *Foreign savings or capital inflows (in foreign currency).
1621   FSAV0 = SAM(SI,RW)/EXR0;
1622   
1623  *Total private savings.
1624   PSAV0 = SUM(EN, SAM(SI,EN)) + SUM(H, SAM(SI,H));
1625   
1626  *Total absorption.
1627   TABS0 = SUM((C,H), SAM(C,H)) + SUM((A,H), SAM(A,H)) + SUM(C, SAM(C,GV)) + SUM(C, SAM(C,SI)) + SUM(C, SAM(C,STK));
1628   
1629  *Government and investment shares of total absorption.
1630   GOVSHR0 = SUM(C, SAM(C,GV))/TABS0;
1631   INVSHR0 = SAM('TOTAL',SI)/TABS0;
1632   
1633   WALRAS0 = 0;
1634   
1635   
1636  *------------------------------------------------------------------
1637  * 1.5.7  Initialize variables
1638  *------------------------------------------------------------------
1639   
1640   CPI.L          = CPI0;
1641   DMPS.L         = DMPS0;
1642   DPI.L          = DPI0;
1643   DTA.L          = DTA0;
1644   DTE.L          = DTE0;
1645   DTF.L          = DTF0;
1646   DTI.L          = DTI0;
1647   DTM.L          = DTM0;
1648   DTQ.L          = DTQ0;
1649   DTV.L          = DTV0;
1650   EG.L           = EG0;
1651   EH.L(H)        = EH0(H);
1652   EXR.L          = EXR0;
1653   FSAV.L         = FSAV0;
1654   GADJ.L         = GADJ0;
1655   GOVSHR.L       = GOVSHR0;
1656   GSAV.L         = GSAV0;
1657   IADJ.L         = IADJ0;
1658   INVSHR.L       = INVSHR0;
1659   MPS.L(INS)     = MPS0(INS);
1660   MPSADJ.L       = MPSADJ0;
1661   PA.L(A)        = PA0(A);
1662   PDD.L(C)       = PDD0(C);
1663   PDS.L(C)       = PDS0(C);
1664   PE.L(C)        = PE0(C);
1665   PINTA.L(A)     = PINTA0(A);
1666   PM.L(C)        = PM0(C);
1667   PQ.L(C)        = PQ0(C);
1668   PSAV.L         = PSAV0;
1669   PVA.L(A)       = PVA0(A);
1670   PX.L(C)        = PX0(C);
1671   PXAC.L(A,C)    = PXAC0(A,C);
1672   TA.L(A)        = TA0(A);
1673   TAADJ.L        = TAADJ0;
1674   TABS.L         = TABS0;
1675   TE.L(C)        = TE0(C);
1676   TEADJ.L        = TEADJ0;
1677   TF.L(F)        = TF0(F);
1678   TFADJ.L        = TFADJ0;
1679   TI.L(INS)      = TI0(INS);
1680   TIADJ.L        = TIADJ0;
1681   TM.L(C)        = TM0(C);
1682   TMADJ.L        = TMADJ0;
1683   TRII.L(INS,INSP) = TRII0(INS,INSP);
1684   TQ.L(C)        = TQ0(C);
1685   TQADJ.L        = TQADJ0;
1686   TV.L(A)        = TV0(A);
1687   TVADJ.L        = TVADJ0;
1688   QA.L(A)        = QA0(A);
1689   QD.L(C)        = QD0(C);
1690   QE.L(C)        = QE0(C);
1691   QF.L(F,A)      = QF0(F,A);
1692   QFS.L(F)       = QFS0(F);
1693   QG.L(C)        = QG0(C);
1694   QH.L(C,H)      = QH0(C,H);
1695   QHA.L(A,H)     = QHA0(A,H);
1696   QINT.L(C,A)    = QINT0(C,A);
1697   QINTA.L(A)     = QINTA0(A);
1698   QINV.L(C)      = QINV0(C);
1699   QM.L(C)        = QM0(C);
1700   QQ.L(C)        = QQ0(C);
1701   QT.L(C)        = QT0(C);
1702   QVA.L(A)       = QVA0(A);
1703   QX.L(C)        = QX0(C);
1704   QXAC.L(A,C)    = QXAC0(A,C);
1705   WALRAS.L       = WALRAS0;
1706   WF.L(F)        = WF0(F);
1707   WFDIST.L(F,A)  = WFDIST0(F,A);
1708   YF.L(F)        = YF0(F);
1709   YG.L           = YG0;
1710   YI.L(INS)      = YI0(INS);
1711   YIF.L(INS,F)   = YIF0(INS,F);
1712   
1713   
1714  *------------------------------------------------------------------
1715  * 1.5.8  Fixing variables not in the model to zero
1716  *------------------------------------------------------------------
1717   
1718   PA.FX(A)$(NOT AA(A))                    = 0;
1719   PDD.FX(C)$(NOT CD(C))                   = 0;
1720   PDS.FX(C)$(NOT CD(C))                   = 0;
1721   PE.FX(C)$(NOT CE(C))                    = 0;
1722   PM.FX(C)$(NOT CM(C))                    = 0;
1723   PVA.FX(A)$(NOT QVA0(A))                 = 0;
1724   PX.FX(C)$(NOT CX(C))                    = 0;
1725   PXAC.FX(A,C)$(NOT SAM(A,C))             = 0;
1726   QA.FX(A)$(NOT AA(A))                    = 0;
1727   QD.FX(C)$(NOT CD(C))                    = 0;
1728   QE.FX(C)$(NOT CE(C))                    = 0;
1729   QF.FX(F,A)$(NOT QF0(F,A))               = 0;
1730   QG.FX(C)$(NOT SAM(C,GV))                = 0;
1731   QH.FX(C,H)$(NOT SAM(C,H))               = 0;
1732   QHA.FX(A,H)$(NOT SAM(A,H))              = 0;
1733   QINT.FX(C,A)$(NOT SAM(C,A))             = 0;
1734   QINV.FX(C)$(NOT SAM(C,SI))              = 0;
1735   QM.FX(C)$(NOT CM(C))                    = 0;
1736   QQ.FX(C)$(NOT (CD(C) OR CM(C)))         = 0;
1737   QT.FX(C)$(NOT CT(C))                    = 0;
1738   QVA.FX(A)$(NOT QVA0(A))                 = 0;
1739   QX.FX(C)$(NOT CX(C))                    = 0;
1740   QXAC.FX(A,C)$(NOT SAM(A,C))             = 0;
1741   TRII.FX(INS,INSP)$(NOT TRII0(INS,INSP)) = 0;
1742   YI.FX(INS)$(NOT YI0(INS))               = 0;
1743   YF.FX(F)$(NOT YF0(F))                   = 0;
1744   YIF.FX(INS,F)$(NOT YIF0(INS,F))         = 0;
1745   
1746   
1747  *------------------------------------------------------------------
1748  * 1.5.9  Base model closures
1749  *------------------------------------------------------------------
1750   
       In the static and dynamic simulation files, the user chooses between alternative closures. These choices take
       precedence over the choices for the base model made in this file. The clearing variables for factor market and macro
       constraint equations are as follows:
       
       FACEQUIL - WF: for each factor, the economywide wage is the market-clearing variable in a setting with perfect factor
       mobility across activities, given fixed factor supplies QFS. Alternative: Various choices depending on FCLOSURE(F).
       
       CURACCBAL - EXR: a flexible exchange rate clears the current account of the RoW given FSAV. Alternative: Fix EXR
       and flex FSAV OR fix both EXR and FSAV and flex PR 
       
       GOVBAL - GSAV: flexible government savings clears the government account, with fixed government demand for
       commodities. All tax rates are fixed.
       
       SAVINVBAL - IADJ: Aggregate real investment adjusts to match aggregate savings (savings drives investment).
       
       CPI is specified as the model numeraire.
       
       Factor market closure assumes full employment with wages endogenous.
1771   
1772  *Factor markets (full employment, wage endogenous).
1773   QFS.FX(F)   = QFS0(F);
1774   WFDIST.FX(F,A) = WFDIST0(F,A);
1775   
1776  *Current account (flexible exchange rate, fixed foreign savings, no premium on parallel market).
1777   FSAV.FX     = FSAV0;
1778   
1779  *Current government balance (fixed consumption demand, fixed tax rates, flexible government savings).
1780   GADJ.FX     = GADJ0;
1781   TAADJ.FX    = TAADJ0;
1782   DTA.FX      = DTA0;
1783   TEADJ.FX    = TEADJ0;
1784   DTE.FX      = DTE0;
1785   TFADJ.FX    = TFADJ0;
1786   DTF.FX      = DTF0;
1787   TIADJ.FX    = TIADJ0;
1788   DTI.FX      = DTI0;
1789   TMADJ.FX    = TMADJ0;
1790   DTM.FX      = DTM0;
1791   TQADJ.FX    = TQADJ0;
1792   DTQ.FX      = DTQ0;
1793   TVADJ.FX    = TVADJ0;
1794   DTV.FX      = DTV0;
1795   
1796  *Savings-investment balance (fixed savings rates, flexible investment demand)
1797   MPSADJ.FX   = MPSADJ0;
1798   DMPS.FX     = DMPS0;
1799   
1800  *Numeraire price
1801   CPI.FX      = CPI0;
1802   
1803  display ERREXPOUT, ERRSAMBAL, rhoq;
1804  *------------------------------------------------------------------
1805  *1.6 Solve the base model
1806  *------------------------------------------------------------------
1807   
       These options are useful for debugging. When checking whether the initial data represent a solution, set LIMROW to a
       value greater than the number of equations and search for three asterisks in the listing file. SOLPRINT=ON provides
       a complete listing file. 
1813   
1814  OPTIONS ITERLIM = 1000, LIMROW = 1000, LIMCOL = 0, SOLPRINT=ON, MCP=PATH, NLP=CONOPT CNS=CONOPT;
1815   
       The HOLDFIXED option converts all variables which are fixed (.FX) into parameters. They are then not solved as part
       of the model. The TOLINFREP parameter sets the tolerance for determinining whether initial values of variables
       represent a solution of the model equations. Whether these initial equation values are printed is determimed by the
       LIMROW option. Equations which are not satsfied to the degree TOLINFREP are printed with three asterisks next to
       their listing.
1823   
1824   STANDCGE.HOLDFIXED  = 1;
1825   STANDCGE.TOLINFREP  = 0.001;
1826   STANDCGE.MCPRHOLDFX = 1;
1827   STANDCGE.SCALEOPT   = 1;
1828   
1829   SOLVE STANDCGE USING MCP;
1830   
1831   
